icers and obstetricians in Mozambique</article-title><source>BJOG</source><year>1996</year><volume>103</volume><fpage>508</fpage><lpage>512</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1471-0528.1996.tb09797.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mbaruku</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Bergstr&#x000f6;m</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Reducing maternal mortality in Kigoma, Tanzania</article-title><source>Health Policy Plann</source><year>1995</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>71</fpage><lpage>78</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/heapol/10.1.71</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>AbouZahr</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Royston</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><source>Maternal Mortality: A global factbook. World Health Organization</source><year>1991</year><publisher-name>Geneva</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dovlo</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Using mid-level cadres as substitutes for internationally mobile health professionals in Africa. A desk review</article-title><source>Human Resources for Health</source><year>2004</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>7</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15207010</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1478-4491-2-7</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gent</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Skeldon</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Skilled migration: Healthcare policy options</article-title><source>Briefing</source><year>2006</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>4</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fenton</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The epidemiology of district surgery in Malawi</article-title><source>East Centr Afr J Surg</source><year>1997</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>33</fpage><lpage>41</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fenton</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Whitty</surname><given-names>CJM</given-names></name><name><surname>Reynolds</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Caesarean section in Malawi: Prospective study of early maternal and perinatal mortality</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>2003</year><volume>327</volume><fpage>587</fpage><lpage>91</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12969922</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/bmj.327.7415.587</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Meyers</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lobis</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Dakkak</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>UN process indicators: key to measuring maternal mortality reduction</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.fmreview.org/FMRpdfs/FMR19/"/></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ratsma</surname><given-names>YEC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Why more mothers die. The confidential enquiries into institutional maternal deaths in the Southern Region of Malawi</article-title><source>Malawi Safe Motherhood Project</source><year>2001</year></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>